@kahyunnam thanks, both inline asks are in 022c8f13d (merged with current main, no conflicts), and the description paragraph on failed downloads is updated.
The subprocess test for the empty-cubin path joins the lock-scope change in the follow-up PR; say so if you want it in this one.
Smoke on Windows arm64 (GB300, a driver that rejects the published cubins): the FP4 MoE call ends in the named RuntimeError without a crash, and the routing cases that need those cubins fail the same way, no process crash. On Linux (GB300) the workspace query and the fused MoE test files pass.
@aleozlx your narrowed version is in as your commit 21beb2e69 with your authorship; could you re-review so the change request clears? CI on the new head is the last gate.
